- Thank you.


00:02:22.286 --> 00:02:24.760
All right, get outta here.
Shit, shower and shave time for me.


00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.429
Hot date tonight?
Little grab-ass under the mistletoe?


00:02:27.529 --> 00:02:30.284
I wish. I'm introducin' my father


00:02:30.384 --> 00:02:31.844
- to some new business partners.
- Oh, yeah?


00:02:31.944 --> 00:02:34.770
Been workin' on it for about nine months
and finally he agrees to hear me out.


00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.641
- Hey, well, he's a busy man, your father.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, no shit.


00:02:38.741 --> 00:02:40.776
- All right. See ya later, fellas.
- All right, see ya.


00:02:40.876 --> 00:02:44.814
- Hey, guys.
- What's up, Jimmy? How you doin'?


00:02:50.986 --> 00:02:53.388
Christ! Can I get one moment to myself?


00:02:53.488 --> 00:02:56.458
- Hey, Danny.
- Hey. What do you want?


00:02:56.558 --> 00:03:00.629
I talked to your father this mornin'
and the heater blew over at my place.


00:03:00.729 --> 00:03:02.431
He told me to ask you about a loan.


00:03:02.531 --> 00:03:03.702
- A loan?
- Yeah.


00:03:03.802 --> 00:03:06.534
- Or a handout?
- Naw, it's just a loan.


00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:09.037
Why he keeps you around, I got no idea.


00:03:09.137 --> 00:03:12.274
- All right. How much do you need?
- About eight hundred.


00:03:12.374 --> 00:03:15.177
I don't know what "about eight hundred"
means, Jimmy. Give me a number.


00:03:16.759 --> 00:03:18.848
- Eight hundred?
- Eight hundred?


00:03:20.622 --> 00:03:22.474
- All right.
- Thanks, Danny.


00:03:22.574 --> 00:03:26.521
Jee... you know... McCauley, he...
the son of a bitch canceled on me.


00:03:27.621 --> 00:03:29.892
I need a Santa for a Christmas
party this afternoon.


00:03:32.928 --> 00:03:34.796
- Santa Claus?
- Yeah.


00:03:35.296 --> 00:03:36.832
- Jeez, Danny, I...
- You'll be great.


00:03:36.932 --> 00:03:40.769
- Find someone else? I gotta get home.
- Yeah. I'll get somebody else.


00:03:41.774 --> 00:03:44.039
You freeze your little nuts off.


00:03:45.539 --> 00:03:46.653
Come on, Danny.


00:04:07.762 --> 00:04:10.747
You see that? You see that switch?
I switch, and then I get out.


00:04:10.847 --> 00:04:11.833
- Yeah.
- And then you're out.


00:04:11.933 --> 00:04:13.976
- You control him with the jab.
- Yeah.


00:04:14.076 --> 00:04:15.016
- All right?
- Right.


00:04:15.116 --> 00:04:18.443
Put the phone down.
Watch me with your own eyes. Okay?


00:04:18.543 --> 00:04:19.868
What the fuck, man?


00:04:24.646 --> 00:04:26.348
Oh, shit! Yo!


00:04:30.985 --> 00:04:32.822
- Yo, look at his face.
- Sorry, man.


00:04:33.622 --> 00:04:35.573
Get the fuck outta here.


00:04:35.673 --> 00:04:38.293
- You started it.
- Walk of shame.


00:04:39.493 --> 00:04:43.231
- Yo, Mike, you knocked him the fuck out.
- What'd I tell you about talkin' like that?


00:04:43.331 --> 00:04:44.904
My bust.


00:04:45.004 --> 00:04:46.734
- See how I kept my elbows tight?
- Yeah, I saw 'em.


00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:49.654
You gotta be careful fighting Garrity.
He's gonna wanna push you against the ropes.


00:04:49.754 --> 00:04:53.309
Just give him one of these.
Knock his shit-talkin' mouth right out.


00:04:54.409 --> 00:04:57.379
- Sorry. It slipped.
- Go ahead, Legs.


00:04:57.479 --> 00:05:00.682
Gonna find out real soon
how fast it can all slip away.


00:05:00.782 --> 00:05:03.021
- Relax, Mike. I was just messing around.
- That's your problem.


00:05:03.121 --> 00:05:06.422
You got all the talent in the world
and all you wanna do is mess around.


00:05:10.591 --> 00:05:14.396
I'm told that you're a man
of influence, Mr. Maguire,


00:05:14.496 --> 00:05:18.800
that nothing moves in or out
of this borough without your approval.


00:05:19.356 --> 00:05:24.773
And my employers are looking for a partner
to help bring our product into the city.


00:05:24.873 --> 00:05:26.475
We use our contacts in the union, pop.


00:05:26.675 --> 00:05:30.445
Three bins a month,
dockworkers know which bins are comin' in


00:05:30.545 --> 00:05:33.882
and all they gotta do is make sure
they pass through without inspection.


00:05:34.482 --> 00:05:36.185
What exactly is your product?


00:05:38.353 --> 00:05:39.854
Heroin.


00:05:40.691 --> 00:05:43.959
99% pure. The very best in the world.


00:05:44.159 --> 00:05:46.428
And my son told you
I'd be interested in this?


00:05:46.828 --> 00:05:48.604
Very interested.


00:05:52.766 --> 00:05:54.769
The business has changed, Mr. Grezda.


00:05:55.269 --> 00:05:58.372
Twenty years ago, I made a living
the same way we all did.


00:05:58.472 --> 00:06:02.774
Couple big scores a year,
but mostly I was a grinder.


00:06:02.874 --> 00:06:05.413
Now, you want to lay down
on a few ballgames, you came to me.


00:06:06.312 --> 00:06:10.202
You want to open up a butcher shop
and the bank said "fuck you" on a loan,


00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:12.471
you came to me.


00:06:12.571 --> 00:06:15.433
You know what that butcher shop
is today?


00:06:15.533 --> 00:06:17.784
- No.
- An applebee's.


00:06:19.794 --> 00:06:21.330
Why are you telling me this?


00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:27.135
Because I've had to adapt to the times.
I am a legitimate businessman now.


00:06:28.837 --> 00:06:33.341
I know your business, Mr. Maguire.
That's why I'm here.


00:06:33.741 --> 00:06:35.842
You're wasting your time.


00:06:35.951 --> 00:06:37.629
Hey, hey. Wait! Come on, now.


00:06:37.729 --> 00:06:42.482
Pop, just listen to what he has to say.
You haven't heard the offer yet.


00:06:42.582 --> 00:06:46.659
Two million dollars up front. After that,
you'll receive 20% of all the product


00:06:46.759 --> 00:06:49.214
you allow to pass safely
through the port.


00:06:49.314 --> 00:06:50.859
The answer's no.


00:06:52.621 --> 00:06:54.029
Take the night to think it over.


00:06:54.129 --> 00:06:58.266
Once you've considered it more carefully,
you'll realize the mistake you are making.


00:06:59.114 --> 00:07:02.837
How do you think I survived
in this business for 35 years?


00:07:02.937 --> 00:07:04.484
Everyone I came up with is either dead


00:07:04.584 --> 00:07:07.070
or locked up in federal prison
waitin' to be buried.


00:07:07.841 --> 00:07:10.454
I don't make mistakes.


00:07:15.082 --> 00:07:16.819
It's Christmas time.


00:07:16.919 --> 00:07:21.056
My friends are here to celebrate with me.
Get the fuck outta my house.


00:07:24.893 --> 00:07:25.969
Take this shit with ya.


00:07:37.104 --> 00:07:38.774
Guys. My old man. I don't even know
what just happened.


00:07:38.874 --> 00:07:41.329
We paid you to guarantee
your father's support.


00:07:41.429 --> 00:07:43.745
Just let me talk to him, all right?
I'll get it all figured out.


00:07:43.845 --> 00:07:47.975
I'll be stopping by your house tonight...
to pick up our money.


00:07:48.075 --> 00:07:51.085
You know what happens
if you don't have it.


00:07:51.185 --> 00:07:54.189
- Merry Christmas.
- Merry Christmas, guys.


00:07:55.256 --> 00:07:57.992
Fucking garbage. I hate Albanians.


00:07:58.142 --> 00:07:59.962
What the fuck was that?


00:08:00.362 --> 00:08:02.564
Did you even listen
to what he had to say?


00:08:02.664 --> 00:08:04.066
That's not our business, Danny.


00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:09.103
Shut your mouth.
I'm talkin' to my father.


00:08:10.471 --> 00:08:13.084
- What's the problem, Danny?
- The problem is...


00:08:13.184 --> 00:08:17.305
all I ever hear outta your mouth
is when am I gonna pull my weight?


00:08:17.545 --> 00:08:19.118
And now I bring you
a piece of business...


00:08:19.218 --> 00:08:21.038
- A good piece of business.
- And you're mad


00:08:21.138 --> 00:08:23.250
- because I let it walk out the door.
- Yeah.


00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:26.254
When I was younger,
somebody made me the same proposal.


00:08:26.354 --> 00:08:28.757
I made so much money
bringing cocaine into the city,


00:08:28.857 --> 00:08:30.876
I had to rent a storage unit
to store all the cash.


00:08:30.976 --> 00:08:33.795
The problem was,
everybody got hooked on the shit.


00:08:34.295 --> 00:08:37.799
I watched my friends rot away in front of me
until I couldn't recognize them anymore.


00:08:38.899 --> 00:08:41.837
I had to kill people I loved
because I couldn't trust them.


00:08:44.504 --> 00:08:47.588
Not enough money in the world
to pull me back in.


00:08:47.688 --> 00:08:50.779
Pop, I made promises to these people.


00:08:50.879 --> 00:08:54.466
- I can't just walk away.
- You made a mess.


00:08:54.566 --> 00:08:57.286
It's time somebody other than me
cleaned it up.


00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:20.979
One, two, three, four, five,


00:09:21.079 --> 00:09:24.729
- Lily, what are you doin' in here?
- I'm hiding from Catelyn.


00:09:24.829 --> 00:09:26.815
...nine, ten.


00:09:29.917 --> 00:09:32.354
- Is she in here?
- Is who in here? She's over there.


00:09:36.524 --> 00:09:38.045
- I see you.
- It doesn't count!


00:09:38.145 --> 00:09:40.061
- You have to tag me!
- I said I see you.


00:09:40.161 --> 00:09:43.465
Doesn't count unless you tag her.
It doesn't count unless you tag her.


00:09:43.565 --> 00:09:44.732
- You didn't touch her.
- Tag!


00:09:44.832 --> 00:09:47.151
- You got tagged.
- Didn't I tell you girls to get ready?


00:09:47.251 --> 00:09:50.839
We're going to your uncle Ricky's house.
Go on. Get your butts in that room.


00:09:51.653 --> 00:09:53.061
- I thought you were off tonight.
- I was.


00:09:53.161 --> 00:09:55.210
Till somebody broke her wrist
fallin' off-a the jungle gym.


00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:56.812
So you're not comin'
to Ricky's for dinner?


00:09:56.912 --> 00:09:59.286
I can pay the hospital bill or go to Ricky's
for dinner. What do you want me to do?


00:09:59.386 --> 00:10:01.483
I want you to do what you promised.
And you said Friday...


00:10:01.583 --> 00:10:04.486
Don't tell me what I said.
I know what I said.


00:10:04.986 --> 00:10:07.827
Fine. I don't want you there anyway
if you're gonna act like an asshole.


00:10:07.927 --> 00:10:10.751
Hey! Come on.


00:10:12.059 --> 00:10:13.261
Hey.


00:10:15.029 --> 00:10:18.831
- Come on. I'm sorry.
- You better be.


00:10:18.931 --> 00:10:20.968
- What're you working on?
- It's for the baby.


00:10:21.068 --> 00:10:24.590
Show him what our lives were like
before he came along. You like it?


00:10:30.284 --> 00:10:33.549
- I'm sorry. I forgot to take it out.
- No, it's all right.


00:10:34.549 --> 00:10:36.017
There.


00:10:36.717 --> 00:10:39.121
Now I won't have to see him
for another five years.


00:10:42.557 --> 00:10:45.047
We want Santa! We want Santa!


00:10:45.147 --> 00:10:46.775
Jimmy?


00:10:48.161 --> 00:10:51.498
- Kids are waitin' for you.
- Yeah, I know. I'm comin'.


00:10:56.905 --> 00:11:01.514
And a bitty baby
and a Barbie power wheels car


00:11:01.614 --> 00:11:04.258
and a Nintendo 3DS.


00:11:04.358 --> 00:11:06.775
- And a hello kitty backpack...
- Yeah.


00:11:07.215 --> 00:11:09.184
Merry Christmas. There you go.


00:11:09.684 --> 00:11:11.269
But I wasn't finished.


00:11:11.369 --> 00:11:15.624
I'll read this on the way back
to the north pole. Okay? There you go.


00:11:15.724 --> 00:11:18.959
Whose idea was it to get Jimmy
to do this thing?


00:11:20.161 --> 00:11:22.597
Okay. Who's next?


00:11:23.852 --> 00:11:26.094
This little girl.


00:11:26.401 --> 00:11:27.736
What's your name, sweetie?


00:11:27.836 --> 00:11:29.137
- Kristen.
- Kristen.


00:11:29.337 --> 00:11:31.873
Mommy? Santa smells funny.


00:11:31.973 --> 00:11:34.675
You think Mommy wants to sit
on Santa's other knee?


00:11:34.775 --> 00:11:39.379
- I think Mommy's a little too big.
- Oh, Santa can make lotsa room on here.


00:11:39.479 --> 00:11:40.923
That's my wife, Jimmy.


00:11:41.623 --> 00:11:44.418
Frank. It's Christmas.


00:11:45.618 --> 00:11:48.739
Gimme a call
if you wanna break the Irish curse.


00:11:49.189 --> 00:11:52.193
I'm skinny, but I'm long.


00:11:53.461 --> 00:11:57.899
Okay... let's see what Santa
brought you this year, Kristie.


00:12:01.937 --> 00:12:05.406
Shit! Fuck! Fucking kids!


00:12:05.606 --> 00:12:07.747
- Jesus Christ!
- Where is he going?


00:12:07.847 --> 00:12:10.111
- Santa'll be right back, kids.
- I didn't get to read my list.


00:12:10.811 --> 00:12:12.447
Get in there!


00:12:12.647 --> 00:12:15.615
Jesus, guy, come on. It's Christmas.


00:12:16.411 --> 00:12:18.526
Oh, God.


00:12:19.734 --> 00:12:22.874
Hey, Pat. When you get done
in there, get him a meal...


00:12:22.974 --> 00:12:25.993
- and some water.
- Come on, Pat, gimme a drink.


00:12:53.053 --> 00:12:55.189
You remember what that's from,
don't you?


00:12:56.339 --> 00:13:00.561
Must have been, what,
the summer of '71? Point Pleasant.


00:13:00.761 --> 00:13:03.096
'70. We enlisted that fall.


00:13:03.196 --> 00:13:07.235
That's right. I was in that bed
with Jenny Blake.


00:13:07.335 --> 00:13:11.505
You were in this one with...
you know, what was that redhead's name?


00:13:11.605 --> 00:13:13.473
- Maureen Galvin.
- Yeah.


00:13:13.573 --> 00:13:16.410
All of a sudden, from downstairs,
my father's voice booms out:


00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:18.580
"Who the hell's
been drinking my scotch?"


00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:21.149
And Jenny, she jumped off me
so fast... bam!


00:13:21.249 --> 00:13:24.686
She smacked her head right
on that thing, knocked herself out.


00:13:29.673 --> 00:13:32.861
- You get enough to eat?
- Yeah, yeah.


00:13:32.961 --> 00:13:34.929
Got plenty left over,
you wanna take some home.


00:13:35.029 --> 00:13:38.033
No. I'm fine.


00:13:38.632 --> 00:13:41.036
Rosie mad at me?


00:13:41.136 --> 00:13:43.705
She'll get over it.


00:13:43.805 --> 00:13:45.080
Gimme a cigarette, will ya?


00:13:46.841 --> 00:13:49.930
She'll think the smell's
coming from you.


00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:02.841
You wanna tell me what's goin' on?


00:14:05.292 --> 00:14:07.560
Come on, Jimmy.


00:14:11.364 --> 00:14:14.402
You look like a goddamn castaway.


00:14:16.757 --> 00:14:19.807
I can't sleep no more, Shawn.


00:14:20.237 --> 00:14:23.011
I keep seeing their faces in my dreams.


00:14:23.261 --> 00:14:26.630
- Whose faces?
- All of 'em.


00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:29.651
Terry Burke. Vince Amato.


00:14:29.751 --> 00:14:32.186
Ernie Hayes.


00:14:33.485 --> 00:14:35.250
It was different then, Jimmy.


00:14:37.692 --> 00:14:39.861
We did what we did because we had to.


00:14:41.361 --> 00:14:42.998
Billy, too.


00:14:43.898 --> 00:14:46.440
I see Billy a lot.


00:14:50.595 --> 00:14:54.009
I got no one left in my life
because of the things I done.


00:14:56.444 --> 00:14:59.480
I chased everyone away.


00:15:01.817 --> 00:15:02.987
Look at me.


00:15:03.818 --> 00:15:06.343
Look at me.


00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:09.623
What do I always tell you?


00:15:10.541 --> 00:15:14.928
Wherever we're going,
when we cross that line,


00:15:15.628 --> 00:15:18.157
we're going together.


00:15:18.967 --> 00:15:20.702
Me and you.


00:15:22.102 --> 00:15:23.971
Me and you.


00:15:25.112 --> 00:15:27.208
- Yeah.
- Yeah.


00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:06.815
Excuse me, buddy,
where the hell are you taking us?


00:16:07.615 --> 00:16:09.924
There's construction
on the Manhattan bridge.


00:16:10.024 --> 00:16:12.320
Traffic's a mess over there,
so I'm tryin' to save you a little time.


00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:15.733
Or make yourself a little more money?


00:16:15.833 --> 00:16:19.361
Trust me, okay?
I lived there my whole life.


00:16:32.873 --> 00:16:36.898
<i>Just one hour away from another chapter
in a historic rivalry</i>


00:16:36.998 --> 00:16:39.603
<i>that is the New Jersey Devils
and the New York Rangers</i>


00:16:39.703 --> 00:16:41.696
<i>at Madison Square Garden in New York.</i>


00:16:41.796 --> 00:16:45.653
<i>It is a crucial game in the eastern
conference standings for both teams.</i>


00:16:45.753 --> 00:16:48.223
Look who it is.


00:16:48.323 --> 00:16:50.508
- You wanna join us?
- I'm expecting someone.


00:16:50.608 --> 00:16:55.129
Bullshit, Jimmy. You don't got any friends.
Detective Torres, meet Jimmy Conlon.


00:16:55.429 --> 00:16:57.461
Jimmy and I spent a lot
of quality time together


00:16:57.561 --> 00:16:59.901
back when he was killing people
for Shawn Maguire.


00:17:00.001 --> 00:17:00.901
Nice to meet you, Jimmy.


00:17:01.001 --> 00:17:05.239
We had a name for him on homicide
task force. Jimmy The Gravedigger.


00:17:06.245 --> 00:17:08.954
What happened to the other guy?
That ginzo?


00:17:09.054 --> 00:17:10.480
- Tornetta.
- Yeah. The ginzo.


00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:15.326
He retired. I guess he got tired of workin'
with a D.A. on Maguire's payroll.


00:17:15.426 --> 00:17:17.485
Tired of watching murderers
like you walk free.


00:17:17.785 --> 00:17:20.287
Maybe you should have taken a bite
outta that pie, Harding.


00:17:20.487 --> 00:17:22.423
You still wouldn't be wearing
suits like that.


00:17:22.523 --> 00:17:25.492
You're breaking my heart.
You don't like my suits.


00:17:25.592 --> 00:17:27.795
What's the number, Jim?


00:17:29.163 --> 00:17:32.032
What's the number?
Tornetta had you at sixteen.


00:17:32.332 --> 00:17:35.296
I always thought it was more.
I made a list once. All the names.


00:17:35.396 --> 00:17:38.106
- How'd that work out?
- Seventeen.


00:17:38.906 --> 00:17:42.076
You see, Tornetta,
he didn't have Ernest Hayes.


00:17:42.976 --> 00:17:46.847
- But that was yours.
- Doesn't ring a bell. Sorry.


00:17:46.947 --> 00:17:48.478
I get a letter from his widow,


00:17:48.978 --> 00:17:52.286
every year, handwritten,
asking me if I got any new information.


00:17:52.386 --> 00:17:55.606
25 years later,
she's still lookin' for closure.


00:17:56.824 --> 00:18:00.177
I got stacks of those letters...
crowdin' my fuckin' desk.


00:18:00.277 --> 00:18:03.361
That get under your skin at all?


00:18:09.088 --> 00:18:12.373
Why don't you whisper it to me.
What's the number, Jim?


00:18:12.773 --> 00:18:14.409
What's the number?


00:18:20.647 --> 00:18:24.852
Tell your partner they don't serve
chimichangas in here.


00:18:25.552 --> 00:18:26.956
You know when the nightmares...


00:18:27.226 --> 00:18:30.219
when they get so bad you can't
look at yourself in the mirror no more,


00:18:30.319 --> 00:18:32.783
you give me a call.


00:18:36.196 --> 00:18:38.766
Let's go. Suddenly I lost my appetite.


00:18:40.501 --> 00:18:43.571
<i>...and we are now less than an hour to go
until the puck drops.</i>


00:18:47.453 --> 00:18:48.584
Get the door.


00:18:52.212 --> 00:18:55.516
- Hey, guys.
- Hey, there the boys are!


00:18:58.926 --> 00:19:01.554
Be gentle. Be gentle.


00:19:01.655 --> 00:19:04.124
You're grabbing
the real weapon there, baby.


00:19:05.451 --> 00:19:08.562
Hey, Danny! My boy!


00:19:08.984 --> 00:19:11.032
- What do you think?
- Nice apartment.


00:19:11.132 --> 00:19:12.266
Come on in. Sit down.


00:19:13.757 --> 00:19:15.987
So, Danny...


00:19:16.437 --> 00:19:18.534
Where's our money?


00:19:19.211 --> 00:19:21.675
You're a businessman.
I like that about you.


00:19:23.638 --> 00:19:26.214
All right. You heard him.
Get him his money.


00:19:29.316 --> 00:19:32.120
<i>In New York City, which means
we're less than twenty minutes to go</i>


00:19:32.220 --> 00:19:34.789
<i>till the opening face-off
between the New York rangers...</i>


00:19:34.889 --> 00:19:38.093
Jesus Christ. Hey, Legs!


00:19:40.194 --> 00:19:42.031
Come here.


00:19:43.031 --> 00:19:45.099
What'd I tell you about riding
around these streets alone?


00:19:45.199 --> 00:19:47.087
I don't gotta answer your questions.
You're not my dad, Mike.


00:19:47.187 --> 00:19:50.638
- So that's how it is between us now.
- Yeah. That's how it is.


00:19:52.338 --> 00:19:54.842
Your mom know you're out here?


00:19:55.242 --> 00:19:58.580
What if I called her? Let her know
you're out here on your own?


00:20:01.211 --> 00:20:05.720
- We have some serious weapons here?
- That's loaded! That's loaded!


00:20:08.922 --> 00:20:10.558
Look. I'll go home
if you give me a ride.


00:20:10.658 --> 00:20:12.459
I can't give you a ride.
I'm with a client right now.


00:20:12.559 --> 00:20:16.064
Come on, Mike. Just let me sit inside.
I ain't never been in a limo before.


00:20:16.164 --> 00:20:18.374
Look. I won't break anything. I promise.


00:20:20.404 --> 00:20:23.004
All right. If I let you inside,
you'll go home straight after?


00:20:23.104 --> 00:20:25.938
- You go home straight after?
- Promise. Straight after.


00:20:27.593 --> 00:20:29.217
Caught him.


00:20:31.379 --> 00:20:33.712
It's all there. Count it.


00:20:42.726 --> 00:20:43.725
Boh!


00:20:44.325 --> 00:20:46.728
- Do you find this funny, Danny?
- Think about what you can do with that money!


00:20:46.838 --> 00:20:49.964
You can put up a luxury high-rise
on park place.


00:20:53.103 --> 00:20:55.269
<i>...so excited at what they can do
in the playoffs...</i>


00:20:56.967 --> 00:20:59.696
Oh, dang, this is my song, Mike.


00:21:03.952 --> 00:21:05.345
Danny.


00:21:07.482 --> 00:21:11.619
Do you have any idea
what we gonna do to you?


00:21:12.119 --> 00:21:13.187
No.


00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:38.945
Look, I'm...


00:21:39.045 --> 00:21:42.715
I'm sorry about what I said earlier.
I was upset with myself, not with you.


00:21:42.815 --> 00:21:44.619
It's all right. I was just worried
you weren't gonna come back.


00:21:44.719 --> 00:21:45.853
I'm not going anywhere.


00:22:08.042 --> 00:22:10.578
Yo, Mike. Mike, check this out.


00:22:13.313 --> 00:22:15.648
Shit. Get down!


00:22:19.787 --> 00:22:22.056
Get outta the car.


00:22:22.156 --> 00:22:24.693
Danny. It's Mike.


00:22:30.497 --> 00:22:33.065
Get out of the car. Get out!


00:22:34.301 --> 00:22:36.477
Fuck.


00:22:36.577 --> 00:22:38.990
Move. Move. Move.


00:23:27.168 --> 00:23:28.323
Shit.


00:24:25.812 --> 00:24:27.582
I found this in his jacket.


00:24:32.168 --> 00:24:33.980
What do we do?


00:24:34.080 --> 00:24:35.556
- Move!
- I think you should call your dad.


00:24:49.022 --> 00:24:52.242
<i>...live and we are ready
for the opening face-off center ice</i>


00:24:52.342 --> 00:24:54.775
<i>at Madison square garden in New York.</i>


00:24:54.875 --> 00:24:57.071
<i>Off the face, New Jersey
in control, Henrique.</i>


00:24:57.171 --> 00:24:59.080
<i>Henrique gives it to Jaromir Jágr,</i>


00:24:59.180 --> 00:25:01.749
<i>and he gets the puck all the way down
near the goal line.</i>


00:25:01.849 --> 00:25:05.419
<i>Sends it in front
and it's cleared out by Lundqvist...</i>


00:25:08.855 --> 00:25:10.757
Hey, Shawn.


00:25:10.857 --> 00:25:13.436
Listen, sorry again about...


00:25:15.696 --> 00:25:17.586
What?


00:25:18.565 --> 00:25:20.567
Michael?


00:25:21.067 --> 00:25:23.109
My Michael?


00:25:25.436 --> 00:25:28.408
Yeah. Yeah. Sure.


00:26:15.289 --> 00:26:18.058
Gabby? Gabby?


00:26:18.558 --> 00:26:20.528
Gabby? Catelyn?


00:26:20.628 --> 00:26:22.630
Lily?


00:26:25.311 --> 00:26:28.713
Tell Danny to stay put
until I hear from Jimmy.


00:26:28.963 --> 00:26:30.716
What about the Albanians?


00:26:30.816 --> 00:26:32.910
It won't be long before they realize
Grezda's not around.


00:26:33.010 --> 00:26:35.384
They'll come after Danny.


00:26:37.912 --> 00:26:42.507
- What are you thinking about?
- The exact moment my son went wrong.


00:26:48.945 --> 00:26:51.364
Hey, Ricky. It's me.
Put Gabby on the phone.


00:26:53.392 --> 00:26:54.668
- <i>Michael?</i>
- Hey.


00:26:54.768 --> 00:26:57.565
Listen. I need you and the girls to stay
at Ricky's until I call you back, okay?


00:26:57.665 --> 00:26:59.800
- <i>What? Why do we have to stay here?</i>
- Gabby?


00:26:59.900 --> 00:27:02.886
- <i>No! Tell me what's going on, Michael!</i>
- Gabby? Goddamn it!


00:27:02.986 --> 00:27:07.018
I don't wanna yell, but it's the only way
I can get through to you! Hello?


00:27:08.462 --> 00:27:10.440
Hello?


00:27:46.753 --> 00:27:49.838
- Can I come in?
- What are you doing here?


00:27:50.117 --> 00:27:52.486
I got a call from Shawn.
You talk to the police yet?


00:27:52.586 --> 00:27:55.455
- Talk to the police about what?
- We both know why I'm here, Michael.


00:27:55.555 --> 00:27:57.324
Now, let's figure this out
so no one else gets hurt.


00:27:57.424 --> 00:28:00.127
You stay out of my house,
you understand me?


00:28:01.115 --> 00:28:03.562
What are you gonna do with that thing?


00:28:16.942 --> 00:28:19.474
So, what, they sent you
to keep me quiet?


00:28:19.574 --> 00:28:22.550
Shawn would...
well, he'd appreciate your support.


00:28:22.650 --> 00:28:24.418
You mean he'd appreciate me
keeping my mouth shut.


00:28:24.518 --> 00:28:27.556
- Yeah.
- Who were they?


00:28:27.656 --> 00:28:29.552
I don't know.


00:28:29.952 --> 00:28:32.806
Whatever Danny did,
I'm sure he had a reason for it.


00:28:32.906 --> 00:28:34.528
You always had a reason?


00:28:35.321 --> 00:28:38.232
Or were you just...
following marchin' orders?


00:28:39.202 --> 00:28:41.168
Let's just get through the night?


00:28:41.568 --> 00:28:45.037
After that, you can go back
to hate me all you want.


00:28:49.309 --> 00:28:50.818
Yeah.


00:28:50.918 --> 00:28:53.079
Yeah, I get it.


00:28:53.179 --> 00:28:55.448
I get it! All right. Yeah.


00:28:55.548 --> 00:28:58.584
No, I'm not goin' nowhere.


00:28:59.651 --> 00:29:02.155
Oh, that's the house here.


00:29:02.755 --> 00:29:05.114
3428 56th Drive. That's it.


00:29:11.832 --> 00:29:15.035
Are you sure you wanna do this?
I mean, your old man told us to stay put.


00:29:15.135 --> 00:29:18.338
He wants me to clean up my mess.
That's exactly what I'm gonna do.


00:29:18.438 --> 00:29:20.019
Well, I think we should wait
for Jimmy to get here.


00:29:20.119 --> 00:29:22.643
Maybe you shouldn't think so much.


00:29:24.978 --> 00:29:26.810
You don't smoke in my house.


00:29:32.952 --> 00:29:35.661
The place looks nice.


00:29:35.761 --> 00:29:39.976
- I haven't been here since...
- Since Mom's funeral.


00:29:40.076 --> 00:29:44.697
- It was nice of you to show up.
- Well, I heard there was free booze.


00:29:48.268 --> 00:29:49.570
It's funny to you.


00:29:50.070 --> 00:29:52.207
- Just trying to be...
- Yeah.


00:29:57.244 --> 00:30:00.247
Five years and it takes Shawn Maguire
for you to come see me.


00:30:00.347 --> 00:30:04.031
- You never wanted me to come see you.
- Because you're trash.


00:30:04.131 --> 00:30:06.987
And I don't want trash around my family.


00:30:07.287 --> 00:30:11.573
They shoulda locked you up a long time ago.
Made you pay for the things you did.


00:30:11.673 --> 00:30:13.434
Just because I'm not
behind bars doesn't mean


00:30:13.534 --> 00:30:17.269
I'm not paying for what I did, Michael.


00:30:41.732 --> 00:30:43.323
So, what happens now?


00:30:43.423 --> 00:30:47.200
I'll go see Shawn.
Let him know we talked.


00:30:47.300 --> 00:30:49.796
I'm sure he'll wanna show
his appreciation.


00:30:49.896 --> 00:30:52.533
A little money
he could set aside for the girls.


00:30:52.933 --> 00:30:54.579
- Catelyn and Lily.
- What's that?


00:30:54.679 --> 00:30:56.670
My daughters' names.


00:30:57.670 --> 00:31:00.825
Catelyn Grace Conlon
and Lily Margaret Conlon.


00:31:00.925 --> 00:31:02.759
I know what their names are.
Do they know mine?


00:31:02.859 --> 00:31:07.447
They don't got a reason to know yours.
You're not a part of their lives.


00:31:07.847 --> 00:31:09.596
It's bad enough you were part of mine.


00:31:15.454 --> 00:31:18.491
- Goodbye, Michael.
- Goodbye, Jimmy.


00:32:12.135 --> 00:32:15.215
Oh, shit. Oh, shit.


00:32:16.296 --> 00:32:18.651
Call an ambulance.


00:32:23.056 --> 00:32:25.268
What are you just standing there for?
Call an ambulance!


00:32:25.368 --> 00:32:28.176
You're wasting your time.


00:32:48.115 --> 00:32:49.716
Hello.


00:32:49.816 --> 00:32:53.820
<i>Yeah. It's me.</i>


00:32:54.353 --> 00:32:55.890
How'd it go with Michael?


00:32:57.957 --> 00:32:59.882
<i>Hello?</i>


00:33:00.359 --> 00:33:03.430
<i>I just killed your boy, Shawn.</i>


00:33:03.930 --> 00:33:06.897
I just killed Danny.


00:33:09.334 --> 00:33:12.144
<i>I had to. He was gonna shoot Michael.</i>


00:33:25.184 --> 00:33:29.220
- Are you sure he's dead?
- Yeah. I'm sure.


00:33:31.191 --> 00:33:33.794
Who is it, honey?


00:33:37.162 --> 00:33:39.845
You know how this has to end.


00:33:41.067 --> 00:33:43.437
Yeah, I know.


00:33:44.937 --> 00:33:46.448
For Michael, too.


00:33:48.448 --> 00:33:49.496
Yeah.


00:33:54.380 --> 00:33:56.095
<i>Hey, Shawn.</i>


00:33:58.795 --> 00:34:02.474
Wherever we're going,
when we cross that line...


00:34:02.922 --> 00:34:05.458
we're going together.


00:34:05.784 --> 00:34:07.194
Right?


00:34:26.366 --> 00:34:27.755
- What are you doing?
- I'm calling the cops.


00:34:27.855 --> 00:34:31.418
You don't wanna do that. Trust me.


00:34:35.187 --> 00:34:36.728
Get out of my house.


00:34:38.258 --> 00:34:42.065
Get out of my house!
Get out of my house!


00:34:43.430 --> 00:34:44.748
Get out!


00:34:58.711 --> 00:35:00.514
<i>911, what's your emergency?</i>


00:35:00.614 --> 00:35:02.179
This is Michael Conlon.


00:35:02.579 --> 00:35:05.267
3428 56th Drive.


00:35:05.367 --> 00:35:08.938
A man's been... shot and killed here.


00:35:09.038 --> 00:35:12.517
- In self-defense.
- <i>Did you shoot the victim?</i>


00:35:14.217 --> 00:35:16.095
No.


00:35:16.595 --> 00:35:18.053
My father did.


00:35:23.615 --> 00:35:26.004
Oh, no.


00:35:42.689 --> 00:35:48.395
<i>Report of a shooting at 3428 56th Drive.
All area units respond. Over.</i>


00:35:51.330 --> 00:35:53.271
- You Michael Conlon?
- Yes, sir.


00:35:53.371 --> 00:35:57.169
- Officers Randle and Colston.
- Come on in.


00:35:59.539 --> 00:36:01.140
I don't know where to start...


00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:04.678
I work as a limousine driver,
and earlier today I picked up a reservation.


00:36:05.578 --> 00:36:07.814
Two gentlemen
at the Gramercy Park Hotel.


00:36:07.914 --> 00:36:11.051
And... and they wanted me
to take them to Ridgewood.


00:36:11.151 --> 00:36:15.120
Lift your arms for me, please.
Lace your fingers together behind your head.


00:36:15.220 --> 00:36:17.925
- Turn around, please.
- Yes, sir.


00:36:19.716 --> 00:36:21.838
What the he...? What the hell?
I'm trying to explain to you.


00:36:21.938 --> 00:36:23.794
You feel that?


00:36:23.894 --> 00:36:26.366
Say another word and I'll blow
your fuckin' teeth out your ear.


00:36:30.637 --> 00:36:33.273
I'm not hiding anything.
I'm trying to explain to you.


00:36:33.373 --> 00:36:37.210
Officer, you're making a fuckin'
mistake here. I'm trying to tell you...


00:36:54.494 --> 00:36:59.032
Six-double-0-five at 3438 56th drive.
That ALS unit en route?


00:36:59.432 --> 00:37:02.296
<i>Ten-four, six-double-0 five.
Westbound on 32nd.</i>


00:37:02.396 --> 00:37:04.682
All right. Let 'em know there's a deceased
white male in the kitchen.


00:37:04.782 --> 00:37:08.275
Neighbors saw an armed suspect
flee the building just before we arrived.


00:37:08.375 --> 00:37:10.710
- What the hell are you talkin' about?
- White male, black sweatpants,


00:37:10.810 --> 00:37:13.090
- black hoodie. Approximately 6'3".
- What the hell you doin', man?


00:37:13.190 --> 00:37:15.892
- Suspect is armed.
- He's lying! I'm in the car!


00:37:15.992 --> 00:37:17.884
We're gonna take a drive around
to see if we can locate him.


00:37:17.984 --> 00:37:20.637
- Hey! Let me outta here!
- <i>Ten-four, six-double-0 five.</i>


00:37:20.737 --> 00:37:23.272
Let me outta here! Let me outta here!


00:37:31.631 --> 00:37:33.826
Where you takin' me?


00:37:43.476 --> 00:37:45.811
Hey, that's Frank.


00:37:46.411 --> 00:37:49.196
He wants us to follow him.


00:38:35.695 --> 00:38:37.377
Get outta here!


00:39:27.525 --> 00:39:29.138
Oh, shit!


00:39:32.585 --> 00:39:34.507
Watch out! Watch out! Watch out!


00:39:54.274 --> 00:39:55.847
He's still comin'.


00:40:20.366 --> 00:40:21.330
Shit!


00:40:47.860 --> 00:40:50.163
He's comin' back.
This fuckin' guy won't quit.


00:40:52.198 --> 00:40:54.733
Watch it! Watch it! Watch it!


00:41:08.621 --> 00:41:10.743
Get back! Get back!


00:41:10.843 --> 00:41:12.912
Get back!


00:41:16.789 --> 00:41:18.348
Mike. Mike!


00:41:20.159 --> 00:41:22.191
My God.


00:41:27.767 --> 00:41:29.097
Cover your face!


00:41:34.406 --> 00:41:36.495
Give me your hands.


00:41:40.479 --> 00:41:42.148
- You okay?
- No! I'm not okay.


00:41:42.248 --> 00:41:44.682
Come on! Let's move!


00:41:52.726 --> 00:41:54.005
Come on.


00:42:00.332 --> 00:42:01.802
Don't do it, son!


00:42:06.805 --> 00:42:09.336
Come on. We gotta move.


00:42:16.115 --> 00:42:18.152
Come on!


00:42:23.431 --> 00:42:26.159
What the fuck?! Hey!


00:42:26.259 --> 00:42:27.926
Hey, asshole!


00:42:28.026 --> 00:42:29.973
Slow down.


00:42:31.865 --> 00:42:34.532
Come on, let's go! Move, move, move!


00:42:44.710 --> 00:42:47.706
- You owe me $2.50, dickhead.
- Back off, pal.


00:42:47.806 --> 00:42:49.734
I'm not gonna back off!
You stole my fare.


00:42:49.834 --> 00:42:51.484
I'm not gonna say it again.


00:42:51.584 --> 00:42:53.335
- Are you kidding?!
- Get lost!


00:42:53.435 --> 00:42:54.923
I'm not gonna get lost.


00:42:55.023 --> 00:42:57.458
- You should at least apologize.
- Look, I'll give ya the money.


00:42:58.358 --> 00:43:01.394
Take it easy, man. Jesus Christ.


00:43:02.433 --> 00:43:04.927
Forget about it. It's just $2.50.


00:44:09.829 --> 00:44:12.586
Hey, Frank. Your wife called me earlier.


00:44:12.686 --> 00:44:15.034
Yeah? What'd she say?


00:44:15.134 --> 00:44:18.427
She wants to take me up on my offer.


00:44:18.527 --> 00:44:21.106
- Is that right?
- I gotta tell ya.


00:44:21.206 --> 00:44:24.844
I've never seen a woman
swallow twelve inches the way she does.


00:44:58.944 --> 00:45:01.516
<i>South entrance clear.</i>


00:45:35.246 --> 00:45:40.497
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, we are being held
momentarily by train traffic ahead of us.</i>


00:45:50.930 --> 00:45:52.981
Jimmy.


00:46:08.247 --> 00:46:10.115
Maria.


00:46:10.215 --> 00:46:13.786
Rose is asleep.
Don't wake her till the mornin'.


00:46:14.986 --> 00:46:17.890
Load the bodies from Danny's
into Michael's limousine.


00:46:17.990 --> 00:46:20.492
Dump the car where the cops can find it.


00:46:20.592 --> 00:46:23.296
Make sure everything points to Michael.


00:46:30.002 --> 00:46:34.407
I know. It's my fault. Every shitty
little thing in your life is my fault, right?


00:46:34.507 --> 00:46:36.475
- I'm turning myself in.
- Not yet, you're not.


00:46:36.875 --> 00:46:38.843
Shawn's gonna come after you, Michael.


00:46:38.943 --> 00:46:41.747
And if he can't get to you,
he's gonna go after your family.


00:46:41.847 --> 00:46:44.150
Right now you've gotta worry
about staying alive.


00:46:44.250 --> 00:46:47.620
And I'm the best chance you've got.
I know how this works.


00:46:47.720 --> 00:46:49.488
I want people at his house.


00:46:49.588 --> 00:46:52.423
<i>Right now, Shawn's got everyone
meeting at the Abbey.</i>


00:46:52.523 --> 00:46:54.760
<i>And from there, they're gonna start
pulling your life apart.</i>


00:46:54.860 --> 00:46:56.795
<i>Friends, family, coworkers.</i>


00:46:56.895 --> 00:46:59.565
- Go!
- Anyone that can connect them to you.


00:47:09.341 --> 00:47:11.677
And the cops?
They've got their own motivation.


00:47:12.432 --> 00:47:14.747
<i>You know what they do to cop killers?</i>


00:47:14.847 --> 00:47:18.082
<i>They don't like to leave it
in a jury's hands.</i>


00:47:20.085 --> 00:47:22.120
Hey, Paul. Yeah.


00:47:22.220 --> 00:47:23.756
- I got what you need.
- Got it.


00:47:24.156 --> 00:47:26.949
Let's go. Woodhaven, Queens.


00:47:27.927 --> 00:47:30.729
There's gotta be a few good cops.
Someone'll listen.


00:47:30.829 --> 00:47:33.465
The good cops won't listen to you
'cause you're my son.


00:47:33.565 --> 00:47:37.403
25 years, I've been chasing this son
of a bitch. This has gotta end tonight.


00:47:37.503 --> 00:47:41.173
<i>And those two bodies from Danny's place,
Shawn will make sure they point back to you.</i>


00:47:41.273 --> 00:47:44.776
<i>This is fourteen-eighty two. We got
a one-eight-seven in the suspect vehicle.</i>


00:47:44.876 --> 00:47:47.612
They just found two bodies
inside of Mike Conlon's limousine.


00:47:47.712 --> 00:47:50.616
Albanians. Part of a gang
that operates out of Brooklyn.


00:47:50.716 --> 00:47:53.953
<i>Right now, we're the most
wanted men in this city.</i>


00:47:54.853 --> 00:47:56.455
Michael, listen to me.


00:47:56.755 --> 00:48:00.960
One night. That's all I'm asking.
Listen to your father for one night.


00:48:01.060 --> 00:48:03.963
If I can't figure this out by the morning,
I'll walk myself into the precinct


00:48:04.063 --> 00:48:06.165
and tell 'em I blew
those two officers away.


00:48:06.765 --> 00:48:09.668
One night. Then you never
have to see me again.


00:48:11.318 --> 00:48:13.340
One night.


00:48:21.079 --> 00:48:23.102
This way.


00:48:38.263 --> 00:48:39.732
- Gimme your lace.
- What?


00:48:39.832 --> 00:48:42.337
Your shoelace. Come on.


00:48:47.206 --> 00:48:48.740
What're you doin'?


00:48:49.140 --> 00:48:52.585
- Where's your family?
- My brother-in law's.


00:48:52.685 --> 00:48:56.048
I want you to drive there.
Make sure they're safe.


00:48:57.009 --> 00:48:59.509
Don't move until you hear from me.


00:49:02.286 --> 00:49:04.168
Wow.


00:49:11.429 --> 00:49:12.431
Where're you gonna go?


00:49:12.531 --> 00:49:16.135
I'm gonna talk to Shawn.
See if we can fix this thing.


00:49:21.405 --> 00:49:23.240
Hey.


00:49:23.964 --> 00:49:26.513
Stay off the main streets. Yeah?


00:49:43.806 --> 00:49:46.265
I'm so sorry, Mr. Maguire.


00:49:47.865 --> 00:49:50.536
I'm so sorry for all of this.


00:49:50.636 --> 00:49:53.105
He was my best friend.


00:49:53.205 --> 00:49:56.675
- I shoulda done something.
- Look at me. Look at me.


00:49:59.010 --> 00:50:00.180
Did he suffer?


00:50:00.680 --> 00:50:02.347
- Danny?
- Did my boy suffer?


00:50:02.647 --> 00:50:07.797
He just kind of went down.
It was real quick.


00:50:08.954 --> 00:50:11.032
Thank you.


00:50:11.991 --> 00:50:17.588
- It's okay. Come here. It's okay.
- Sorry, I didn't want him to die.


00:50:37.450 --> 00:50:41.487
- Did anybody see who killed the cop?
- Witness couldn't identify the shooter.


00:50:41.587 --> 00:50:45.157
Conlon and the son were both seen
pulling their weapons.


00:50:46.392 --> 00:50:48.660
- They couldn't get to Michael.
- I know.


00:50:48.960 --> 00:50:52.598
Jimmy called. He wants to meet
in the old neighborhood.


00:50:58.537 --> 00:50:59.538
You need to see this.


00:50:59.638 --> 00:51:03.725
<i>A city-wide manhunt is underway tonight
as police search for two suspects</i>


00:51:03.825 --> 00:51:06.762
<i>identified as James Conlon
and his son, Michael Conlon,</i>


00:51:06.862 --> 00:51:09.231
<i>who they say took the lives
of two police officers</i>


00:51:09.331 --> 00:51:12.151
<i>during a deadly chase
on Jamaica Avenue earlier.</i>


00:51:12.251 --> 00:51:15.787
<i>We're also getting reports tonight the two
could be linked to a double homicide.</i>


00:51:16.287 --> 00:51:18.857
<i>Two bodies were discovered
inside a limousine</i>


00:51:18.957 --> 00:51:21.677
<i>believed to have been driven
by Michael Conlon.</i>


00:51:22.327 --> 00:51:25.197
- What do you got?
- Just got off with the dispatcher.


00:51:25.297 --> 00:51:29.267
Last contact she had with the patrol car
was at 3428 56th Drive.


00:51:29.367 --> 00:51:32.639
Officers responded to a report
of a shooting at Michael Conlon's house.


00:51:32.739 --> 00:51:36.408
Do you wanna guess who the victim is?
Danny Maguire.


00:51:36.508 --> 00:51:40.574
Michael Conlon told the officers
his father was the one who killed him.


00:51:42.514 --> 00:51:43.832
- Harding.
- <i>Evening, Detective.</i>


00:51:43.932 --> 00:51:46.485
This is Jimmy Conlon.


00:51:46.585 --> 00:51:50.067
You got some fuckin' nerve.
You better be on a plane to Shangri-La.


00:51:50.167 --> 00:51:51.961
I tried. Flight was full.


00:51:52.061 --> 00:51:55.560
I got fifteen witnesses that say
you ran a cop car at Jamaica Avenue


00:51:55.960 --> 00:51:59.364
killin' an officer,
while your son killed his partner.


00:52:00.374 --> 00:52:03.602
- I killed that cop. Not Michael.
- <i>Bullshit.</i>


00:52:03.702 --> 00:52:07.348
<i>If your son's anything like you, he was
probably laughing when he pulled the trigger.</i>


00:52:07.673 --> 00:52:09.642
I need your help.


00:52:10.742 --> 00:52:14.830
I am the last person on this earth
that you should be asking help from.


00:52:14.930 --> 00:52:17.983
You're the only cop I can trust.


00:52:20.785 --> 00:52:24.277
- And what's in it for me?
- I'll turn myself in,


00:52:24.377 --> 00:52:27.960
confess to killing those cops,
if you agree to help Michael.


00:52:28.560 --> 00:52:30.238
<i>I'll die in a prison cell.</i>


00:52:30.338 --> 00:52:32.554
That's what you always wanted,
right, Harding?


00:52:32.654 --> 00:52:36.352
You're gonna die in a prison cell anyway,
Conlon. There's no way out this time.


00:52:36.452 --> 00:52:39.758
And I'm pretty sure that I can find
a witness that says your boy did it.


00:52:40.945 --> 00:52:45.628
- Tell me what you want.
- Names. All of them.


00:52:45.728 --> 00:52:47.980
Every life you took.
Every family you ruined.


00:52:48.580 --> 00:52:50.715
<i>If you give me that...</i>


00:52:50.815 --> 00:52:54.420
maybe, fuckin' maybe,
I'll listen to your son.


00:52:56.797 --> 00:52:58.524
Not yet. I need to take care
of a few things.


00:52:58.624 --> 00:53:00.927
- Turn yourself in.
- You drink coffee, Harding?


00:53:01.627 --> 00:53:04.729
Yeah. Six cups a day
for the last thirty years.


00:53:04.829 --> 00:53:08.100
Put in a little extra sugar.
It's gonna be a long night.


00:53:26.321 --> 00:53:27.820
- Gabby? Where are the girls?
- What happened to your face?


00:53:27.920 --> 00:53:30.289
- They're asleep upstairs.
- Hurry up and go pack their stuff.


00:53:30.889 --> 00:53:32.057
Why do you have a gun?


00:53:32.157 --> 00:53:34.460
Look, Michael, whatever
you're going through, there's a way out.


00:53:34.560 --> 00:53:36.328
- Mike. Mike.
- Look, Michael, we get...


00:53:36.428 --> 00:53:38.230
- Sit down, Ricky.
- They said you killed two cops.


00:53:38.330 --> 00:53:40.866
It's all over the news.
Tell me you didn't do it.


00:53:40.966 --> 00:53:44.169
I picked up two clients today,
took 'em to Danny Maguire's house.


00:53:44.269 --> 00:53:45.504
And he killed 'em, he shot 'em both,


00:53:45.604 --> 00:53:47.739
and then he tried to kill me, too,
'cause I saw him do it.


00:53:48.239 --> 00:53:49.261
Did you call the cops?


00:53:49.361 --> 00:53:51.228
- It's not that simple.
- What do you mean it's not that simple?


00:53:51.328 --> 00:53:54.547
Look, I grew up around this stuff.
I know what these people are capable of.


00:53:55.258 --> 00:53:57.082
And now they're comin' after us.


00:53:58.194 --> 00:54:00.086
You gotta take the girls and go.


00:54:00.486 --> 00:54:03.258
- I'm calling the cops.
- Baby. Baby, baby. Baby.


00:54:06.433 --> 00:54:08.937
I'm gonna fix this.


00:54:09.037 --> 00:54:10.667
But you gotta trust me.


00:54:14.605 --> 00:54:17.235
Okay. You gotta tell 'em
you haven't seen us.


00:54:17.335 --> 00:54:20.816
- Do I have to?
- They're not gonna just go away, Ricky.


00:54:22.507 --> 00:54:24.242
Open the goddamn door!


00:54:26.745 --> 00:54:28.839
Can I help you?


00:54:31.616 --> 00:54:33.385
Okay. Come here, sweetie. Come here.


00:54:33.485 --> 00:54:36.422
- Where we going, Daddy?
- We're gonna play hide-and-seek.


00:54:36.622 --> 00:54:39.166
Where do you think you're goin'?!


00:54:41.059 --> 00:54:45.429
Be real quiet, okay?
Uncle Ricky's gonna try to find us.


00:54:54.923 --> 00:54:58.781
Can I help you find something
in my house?


00:55:03.992 --> 00:55:07.819
- Who was here for dinner?
- Just some work friends.


00:55:09.321 --> 00:55:11.156
You always serve your friends
chicken nuggets?


00:55:11.256 --> 00:55:13.769
We're on a budget.


00:55:16.068 --> 00:55:17.356
Where's your friend?


00:55:21.399 --> 00:55:25.439
- I know your sister called.
- What are you, stalking me?


00:55:31.060 --> 00:55:34.345
- What did she want?
- She was cooking dinner.


00:55:39.984 --> 00:55:42.974
She asked about a recipe.


00:55:53.231 --> 00:55:55.262
A recipe?


00:55:55.784 --> 00:55:57.104
Chicken nuggets?


00:56:06.728 --> 00:56:08.414
I'm calling the cops.


00:56:10.582 --> 00:56:12.644
Call 'em now.


00:56:16.288 --> 00:56:17.870
Yeah?


00:56:18.289 --> 00:56:20.792
Okay. I got it.


00:56:25.295 --> 00:56:27.848
Tommy! We gotta go!


00:56:31.904 --> 00:56:33.203
Be quiet.


00:56:44.115 --> 00:56:45.884
They just left.


00:56:46.184 --> 00:56:49.521
It doesn't count! You have to tag me!


00:57:20.118 --> 00:57:22.900
Driver, pull over. Turn off the lights.


00:57:25.856 --> 00:57:29.395
Anyone gives you shit, your transmission
blew and you're waitin' for a backup.


00:57:39.937 --> 00:57:41.407
Hey.


00:57:41.707 --> 00:57:44.409
- You want a drink?
- Nah.


00:57:44.509 --> 00:57:45.911
Don't make me drink alone.


00:57:46.011 --> 00:57:50.242
- Miss, get him a scotch, will you?
- On the rocks.


00:57:50.342 --> 00:57:54.686
So I heard you... left Frank
face-down in the subway.


00:57:54.786 --> 00:57:57.722
- Frank was an asshole.
- Frank had 15 years and 30 pounds on ya.


00:57:57.822 --> 00:58:00.559
- I thought he woulda worn you down.
- So did I.


00:58:03.128 --> 00:58:05.797
- <i>Gomez shoots...</i>
- Close game.


00:58:05.897 --> 00:58:07.532
<i>Coming up on two minutes to go...</i>


00:58:07.832 --> 00:58:11.470
It's gotta be fifteen years since I've been
in here. The place looks different.


00:58:11.570 --> 00:58:14.772
All the old places look different now.


00:58:14.872 --> 00:58:17.341
Me, Richie Ryan, Mickey Featherstone


00:58:17.441 --> 00:58:20.249
would meet every Saturday night
for drinks.


00:58:20.349 --> 00:58:22.175
Sit in that back booth, back there.


00:58:22.275 --> 00:58:27.883
Yeah, I used to bring Danny here
when he was a boy. Special occasions.


00:58:27.983 --> 00:58:30.955
His first communion,
I ordered him a lobster.


00:58:31.055 --> 00:58:35.060
Waitress brings it out.
Big as this table. Beautiful, too.


00:58:35.160 --> 00:58:37.929
He takes a look at it, and he says,


00:58:38.029 --> 00:58:40.840
"do you have any chicken fingers?"


00:58:44.301 --> 00:58:46.070
Thanks.


00:58:46.170 --> 00:58:47.708
How's Rosie?


00:58:49.639 --> 00:58:53.179
Hell of a thing to know you're never gonna
make the woman you love happy again.


00:59:10.695 --> 00:59:14.533
I'm here asking
for my son's life, Shawn.


00:59:15.033 --> 00:59:17.668
I pulled the trigger. I killed Danny.


00:59:17.768 --> 00:59:20.405
You wanna send someone for me,
tell me when.


00:59:20.505 --> 00:59:22.874
I'll keep the door open,
I'll put my gun on the table.


00:59:24.174 --> 00:59:26.166
Michael...


00:59:26.266 --> 00:59:30.048
he's a good kid. He's got a family.
He don't deserve this.


00:59:30.148 --> 00:59:32.718
Michael was not gonna talk.
If Danny hadn't shown up...


00:59:32.818 --> 00:59:36.155
You think I sent him there? I told him
to stay put. He wouldn't listen.


00:59:36.255 --> 00:59:40.759
- He was into some bad shit, Shawn.
- Don't talk to me about my son.


00:59:45.662 --> 00:59:49.038
I'm gonna do what I have to do
to protect Michael.


00:59:49.138 --> 00:59:51.203
If that means I gotta talk to someone...


00:59:51.303 --> 00:59:54.273
- Talk to someone?
- Cops. John Harding.


00:59:54.573 --> 00:59:58.276
- The things I know.
- Things that mattered twenty years ago?


00:59:58.376 --> 01:00:02.213
What, you think the feds are parked
outside, listenin' to this conversation?


01:00:02.313 --> 01:00:06.185
Take a look out there. Nobody gives
a shit about what you know anymore.


01:00:07.285 --> 01:00:08.899
Nobody gives a shit about you.


01:00:08.999 --> 01:00:11.757
You die tomorrow, you'd rot away
alone in your bedroom


01:00:11.857 --> 01:00:15.747
until the stench gets so bad the neighbors
got no choice but to call the cops.


01:00:15.847 --> 01:00:18.764
Wouldn't be any point in having a funeral
because no one would come.


01:00:19.164 --> 01:00:22.333
<i>He shoots! Forty seconds to go.
Kick save by Lundqvist.</i>


01:00:22.433 --> 01:00:25.169
I'm the only one ever cared about you.


01:00:25.269 --> 01:00:29.649
And all of that ended an hour ago
when you killed my son.


01:00:32.911 --> 01:00:35.781
I'm comin' after your boy
with everything I got.


01:00:36.181 --> 01:00:39.051
- I won't let you take him, Shawn.
- You got no choice.


01:00:39.951 --> 01:00:42.453
And when it's done, and it will be done,


01:00:42.553 --> 01:00:44.989
you and I are gonna meet
back here at this restaurant,


01:00:45.089 --> 01:00:47.226
at this same table that I used
to share with my boy,


01:00:47.326 --> 01:00:48.432
and I'm gonna look you in the eyes,


01:00:48.532 --> 01:00:51.680
just like you're looking me
in the eyes right now,


01:00:51.780 --> 01:00:55.834
and I'm gonna see how empty they are


01:00:55.934 --> 01:00:58.403
without your son in the world.


01:00:59.203 --> 01:01:02.107
Same thing I saw in my wife's eyes.


01:01:02.207 --> 01:01:04.938
Same thing you're seein' in my eyes.


01:01:05.127 --> 01:01:07.346
And when I see that...


01:01:08.838 --> 01:01:11.341
then I'll let you die.


01:01:12.418 --> 01:01:16.021
<i>Lundqvist couldn't get his stick on it.
And it just missed. Two, one...</i>


01:01:16.121 --> 01:01:21.376
<i>And it is over at the Garden.
The Rangers win it 3-2.</i>


01:01:21.476 --> 01:01:23.642
Thanks for the drink.


01:01:27.732 --> 01:01:30.256
Where do you think you're going?


01:02:06.304 --> 01:02:07.205
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Easy.


01:02:07.305 --> 01:02:09.340
I left my wallet in my seat.
I'm leaving town tomorrow.


01:02:09.440 --> 01:02:12.577
- I'm screwed without it. Please.
- All right. Take this guy down to his seat.


01:02:12.677 --> 01:02:13.612
- Thanks, pal.
- All right.


01:02:13.712 --> 01:02:16.849
Easy, fellas. Game's over.
No re-entry. Sorry.


01:02:17.749 --> 01:02:20.285
- Sir!
- I got it! Thank you!


01:03:00.024 --> 01:03:01.993
- What'd he say?
- You need to get your family out.


01:03:02.093 --> 01:03:04.337
Remember the cabin I used
to bring you to when you were a boy?


01:03:04.437 --> 01:03:07.838
Up by north-south shore? Take the
throughway all the way up to Haines falls.


01:03:07.938 --> 01:03:09.303
- Yeah.
- You'll be safe there.


01:03:09.703 --> 01:03:11.106
Stay here.


01:03:34.858 --> 01:03:37.863
Yeah, that's... that's Danny.


01:03:41.198 --> 01:03:43.534
That's my son.


01:03:50.441 --> 01:03:51.943
Who's that man, Daddy?


01:03:53.043 --> 01:03:55.081
It's nobody, honey.
Let's get in the car.


01:03:58.082 --> 01:04:01.652
- You know where you're going?
- I'll find it.


01:04:03.054 --> 01:04:07.292
Hey, babe. Look at me.
It's gonna be okay. Go.


01:04:07.692 --> 01:04:10.328
What're you doing? Get in the car.


01:04:10.528 --> 01:04:13.865
- If I run now, I'll never stop running.
- Michael. You have to leave the city.


01:04:13.965 --> 01:04:15.731
There's this kid I train
down at the boxing gym.


01:04:15.831 --> 01:04:18.490
He was with me in the car
at Danny's house. He saw everything.


01:04:18.590 --> 01:04:21.268
Can you keep me alive
long enough to get to him?


01:04:21.368 --> 01:04:23.174
I'll drive.


01:04:35.686 --> 01:04:38.241
Get me Price.


01:04:41.358 --> 01:04:43.795
So you keep in touch
with your mom's side of the family?


01:04:44.195 --> 01:04:46.431
What, you're the big
family supporter now?


01:04:46.831 --> 01:04:49.967
Listen, I came home a few times.
Your mom and I tried to work things out.


01:04:50.067 --> 01:04:52.704
The only time you ever came home
was when you needed a place to lay low.


01:04:52.804 --> 01:04:55.473
And I'd find a gun
hidden in every room in the house.


01:04:55.873 --> 01:04:59.378
And I'd be scared to death
that you'd end up like cousin Billy.


01:05:05.248 --> 01:05:08.053
- This is Price.
- <i>I got a job for you.</i>


01:05:08.453 --> 01:05:12.390
Two people. I'll double your quote.
But it's gotta be done by the morning.


01:05:12.490 --> 01:05:15.994
They killed two cops and a couple
of squarehead gangsters in Queens.


01:05:16.094 --> 01:05:20.231
The whole city's huntin' 'em down.
I need you to get there first.


01:05:20.531 --> 01:05:21.832
What are their names?


01:05:23.355 --> 01:05:25.803
Michael and Jimmy Conlon.


01:05:25.903 --> 01:05:28.673
- <i>You're fuckin' with me, right?</i>
- You want the job or not?


01:05:28.773 --> 01:05:32.877
<i>Conlon? I'll kill
that motherfucker for free.</i>


01:05:33.477 --> 01:05:36.776
Just make sure his son dies first.


01:05:38.049 --> 01:05:42.087
Your next one, is it a...
a boy or a girl?


01:05:42.687 --> 01:05:44.312
A boy.


01:05:44.412 --> 01:05:47.124
Boy? Got a name picked out?


01:05:47.224 --> 01:05:49.098
Yeah.


01:05:55.368 --> 01:05:57.535
You like what you do,
driving a limo around?


01:05:57.635 --> 01:06:00.204
Sure. I do cartwheels on my way
out the door every night.


01:06:00.304 --> 01:06:01.273
That bad?


01:06:01.373 --> 01:06:03.207
Since when do you give a shit
if I'm happy?


01:06:03.307 --> 01:06:06.577
This is for your own sake, right? I say
I'm happy, that life turned out all right


01:06:06.677 --> 01:06:08.513
and then you don't feel
so guilty about leaving.


01:06:08.613 --> 01:06:10.315
- That's right.
- Yeah.


01:06:10.415 --> 01:06:12.916
So, are you?


01:06:13.223 --> 01:06:15.287
I'd be happier
if I were still fightin', but...


01:06:15.387 --> 01:06:19.057
- I used to watch your fights.
- That's fuckin' bullshit.


01:06:19.157 --> 01:06:21.893
Over on Church Street.
I'd stand in the tunnel.


01:06:21.993 --> 01:06:24.897
I was there when you lost to Ramirez.


01:06:24.997 --> 01:06:27.699
You didn't have the killer instinct
to make a top-class fighter, Mike.


01:06:27.799 --> 01:06:30.534
- I got fucked by the judges.
- The judges didn't fuck you.


01:06:30.734 --> 01:06:33.638
You were ahead at the end of the fourth,
and you stopped using your jab.


01:06:33.938 --> 01:06:36.741
You could've made the rankings
if you'd've used that jab more.


01:06:36.841 --> 01:06:38.810
That's life.
It don't offer any do-overs.


01:06:38.910 --> 01:06:42.013
Believe me, I know. Otherwise,
I would've put in for one a long time ago.


01:06:42.113 --> 01:06:45.483
- You've got a lot of anger in you.
- Wouldn't you? With you as a father?


01:06:45.883 --> 01:06:49.587
Because I left? You got it backwards.


01:06:49.687 --> 01:06:52.257
The things I did, the things I seen...


01:06:52.357 --> 01:06:56.627
it becomes who you are.
You can't just go home and scrub it off.


01:06:56.727 --> 01:06:59.231
The only way I could protect you
was to walk away.


01:06:59.331 --> 01:07:01.333
Forget about you and your mom.


01:07:01.433 --> 01:07:04.837
I wanted a better life for you
than the one I chose for myself.


01:07:08.571 --> 01:07:10.465
That's it.


01:07:17.714 --> 01:07:20.251
I'm sorry, Michael.


01:08:22.014 --> 01:08:25.483
Hey. You know this kid called Legs?
You know where he lives?


01:08:27.181 --> 01:08:28.636
- Building three.
- Which apartment?


01:08:28.736 --> 01:08:31.758
- What do I look like, Google maps?
- Thanks.


01:08:33.891 --> 01:08:35.626
His name's Curtis Banks.


01:08:35.726 --> 01:08:39.531
- You know, his mom works as a nurse.
- No, sorry.


01:08:42.632 --> 01:08:44.368
- Yeah?
- I'm lookin' for Legs.


01:08:44.468 --> 01:08:47.737
Yeah. Me too. Preferably spread.


01:08:56.280 --> 01:08:57.339
Hello?


01:09:04.988 --> 01:09:09.176
- <i>911. What's your emergency?</i>
- Yes. The bad guys that was on the TV?


01:09:09.276 --> 01:09:11.780
- They're outside the door.
- <i>Just hold the line.</i>


01:09:22.106 --> 01:09:26.844
<i>All units respond to a code one. Positive
I.D. on the I-278 shooting suspects.</i>


01:09:26.944 --> 01:09:29.957
<i>648 Park Avenue,
Marcy Houses, building three.</i>


01:09:36.820 --> 01:09:40.081
Hi. I'm lookin' for this kid
called Curtis Banks?


01:09:48.666 --> 01:09:50.869
Open the door, please.


01:09:52.970 --> 01:09:55.273
- He not ready. He not ready.
- No, you not ready.


01:09:55.373 --> 01:09:58.375
- Terrell is gettin' his ass beat.
- Boy, you see!


01:09:58.893 --> 01:10:02.323
Yo, go get the door. Hurry up.


01:10:02.547 --> 01:10:03.415
Yeah?


01:10:03.515 --> 01:10:06.037
- I'm lookin' for this kid Legs, or Curtis.
- Who are you?


01:10:06.137 --> 01:10:07.683
It doesn't matter who we are.
Do you know him or not?


01:10:07.783 --> 01:10:10.154
Sorry, but my mom told me
not to talk to creepy-ass old men.


01:10:10.254 --> 01:10:13.508
Hey. You. I seen you before.
Down at the boxing gym.


01:10:13.608 --> 01:10:16.660
- You know Legs, right?
- Yeah, that's my brother. Is he okay?


01:10:16.760 --> 01:10:18.296
I need to get ahold of him.
It's really important.


01:10:18.396 --> 01:10:20.365
He's not answering his phone.
Where would he go?


01:10:20.465 --> 01:10:23.133
- I don't know.
- Well, think.


01:10:28.539 --> 01:10:31.717
I need you to tell your brother
that Mike needs his help.


01:10:34.312 --> 01:10:37.049
- It's really important.
- All right.


01:10:45.422 --> 01:10:48.624
- <i>Let's go!</i>
- We gotta get out of here.


01:10:48.724 --> 01:10:52.730
It's a big building.
We've got some time. Let's wait.


01:11:16.187 --> 01:11:17.989
<i>We're looking for a white male,
in his thirties...</i>


01:11:18.089 --> 01:11:21.725
- Anybody in there?
- Open the door, please.


01:11:24.361 --> 01:11:26.998
- Let's go. Everybody out.
- Come on, folks. Let's go.


01:11:28.399 --> 01:11:30.802
Police! We need to evacuate
this building.


01:11:32.002 --> 01:11:34.015
Everybody out!


01:11:40.044 --> 01:11:42.580
Copy that. I'm covering the southeast...
Sir! You can't be back here.


01:11:42.680 --> 01:11:46.183
You don't understand. My mom lives
in this building. She's having chest pains.


01:11:46.283 --> 01:11:48.425
There's two fugitives hiding in the building.
I'm not allowed to let anyone in.


01:11:48.525 --> 01:11:51.225
Could you check on her for me?


01:11:51.327 --> 01:11:54.926
- What's her apartment number?
- 317. I have the keys right here.


01:12:03.033 --> 01:12:06.038
- Two tactical units are heading inside now.
- And you're sure Conlon's in there?


01:12:06.138 --> 01:12:08.506
Why do you think I saved you
a front-row seat?


01:12:18.515 --> 01:12:20.118
Open up! Police!


01:12:29.961 --> 01:12:30.861
Shit.


01:12:30.961 --> 01:12:33.464
- What's goin' on?
- Now's our chance.


01:12:36.033 --> 01:12:37.602
Let's move.


01:12:49.714 --> 01:12:52.316
Fools are in there! He's got a gun!


01:12:52.516 --> 01:12:55.453
- Get back! Get back!
- Move! Freeze!


01:12:56.839 --> 01:12:58.674
Freeze!


01:13:01.008 --> 01:13:03.443
<i>Targets are on the twelfth floor,
headin' down the west stairwell.</i>


01:13:03.543 --> 01:13:06.069
<i>Repeat, twelfth floor.</i>


01:13:15.072 --> 01:13:17.075
Let's go! Let's clear 'em out!


01:13:23.781 --> 01:13:27.836
<i>Shots fired in the west stairwell.
Two officers down!</i>


01:13:34.042 --> 01:13:36.622
Holy shit!


01:13:40.631 --> 01:13:44.702
<i>Attention. An emergency
has been reported in this building.</i>


01:13:44.802 --> 01:13:49.592
<i>Repeat: Do not use elevators.
Please leave the building.</i>


01:13:49.692 --> 01:13:51.710
We gotta get everybody
outta this building now!


01:13:55.645 --> 01:13:58.446
This is some bullshit.


01:14:01.452 --> 01:14:03.021
Shit.


01:14:04.628 --> 01:14:07.691
Easy does it. Okay.


01:14:08.240 --> 01:14:10.247
Move!


01:14:11.462 --> 01:14:13.398
<i>Do not use elevators.</i>


01:14:15.599 --> 01:14:17.766
Shit! He's got a gun!


01:14:19.003 --> 01:14:21.772
<i>Please leave the building, utilizing...</i>


01:14:26.009 --> 01:14:28.338
You ever wanna see your family
again, leave. Leave now.


01:14:28.438 --> 01:14:30.815
- Who was that?
- He's a professional killer.


01:14:30.915 --> 01:14:33.748
He won't stop until we're all dead.


01:14:35.288 --> 01:14:37.806
Go, Mike. Go!


01:14:40.088 --> 01:14:43.927
Hey! Price! Come on, you fucker!


01:14:47.273 --> 01:14:49.668
Come on, Price! You dumb fuck!


01:16:39.809 --> 01:16:41.796
Don't do it, Michael.


01:16:43.714 --> 01:16:45.149
Don't do it!


01:16:47.984 --> 01:16:49.153
- Don't fuckin' move!
- Let's go!


01:16:49.253 --> 01:16:51.322
- Police!
- Freeze! On the ground!


01:16:55.626 --> 01:16:57.055
All right, we're comin' down.


01:17:02.799 --> 01:17:04.472
Conlon!


01:17:04.572 --> 01:17:06.637
Conlon! Stay there, Conlon!


01:17:10.908 --> 01:17:13.546
Goddamn it, Conlon!


01:17:16.146 --> 01:17:18.294
Conlon!


01:17:23.119 --> 01:17:24.655
Stay back.


01:17:24.755 --> 01:17:26.356
Conlon!


01:17:26.456 --> 01:17:28.926
- Come on.
- Hey! Jesus, Conlon.


01:17:29.026 --> 01:17:31.729
Come back up. Come on.
I'll give you a hand.


01:17:36.800 --> 01:17:38.535
They're inside on the ground floor!


01:17:40.171 --> 01:17:42.328
I want them in custody.


01:17:42.873 --> 01:17:44.362
Easy. Easy.


01:17:47.011 --> 01:17:51.349
- <i>Get on the ground! Put your hands up!</i>
- <i>Suspects heading north toward the rail yard.</i>


01:17:51.449 --> 01:17:54.321
<i>We have the area surrounded!</i>


01:18:00.324 --> 01:18:02.265
Get on the ground!


01:18:03.527 --> 01:18:05.196
Freeze!


01:18:05.796 --> 01:18:08.232
Don't fuckin' move!


01:18:08.332 --> 01:18:10.200
Hold it right there!


01:18:10.300 --> 01:18:11.906
<i>Eyes on the suspects.</i>


01:18:12.006 --> 01:18:14.773
<i>Headed to the east quadrant!</i>


01:18:16.440 --> 01:18:17.660
<i>I lost visual.</i>


01:18:19.475 --> 01:18:23.381
<i>Conlon, it's Harding.
It's over. Do ya hear me?</i>


01:18:24.697 --> 01:18:27.217
<i>You gotta surrender.</i>


01:18:33.079 --> 01:18:35.375
<i>That's it. We're comin' in.</i>


01:18:45.601 --> 01:18:46.871
He's not in here.


01:18:47.271 --> 01:18:49.921
Is he fuckin' here?!


01:18:56.779 --> 01:18:59.289
You can't ever pull that trigger.
You understand me?


01:18:59.389 --> 01:19:01.819
You pull that trigger,
you're no better than I am.


01:19:02.019 --> 01:19:04.889
We get everybody to go back
to the edge of the perimeter,


01:19:04.989 --> 01:19:07.591
and we work our way back in.


01:19:07.691 --> 01:19:10.756
We'll go to your uncle Eddie's house.
Come on.


01:19:56.072 --> 01:19:57.541
- Hey, uncle Eddie.
- Michael.


01:19:57.641 --> 01:19:59.479
Just pull the sleeve.


01:20:06.149 --> 01:20:08.156
I got it.


01:20:17.782 --> 01:20:19.730
Don't wipe off the tattoo.


01:20:21.932 --> 01:20:23.233
Thanks.


01:20:23.533 --> 01:20:25.236
There you go.


01:20:25.949 --> 01:20:28.171
What the hell happened to you?


01:20:28.271 --> 01:20:31.309
We were jumped. Over on Bedford Avenue.


01:20:31.409 --> 01:20:34.458
One of 'em had a knife this long.


01:20:34.878 --> 01:20:37.632
Took my wallet, too.


01:20:37.732 --> 01:20:39.750
Where's Mom? Is she asleep?


01:20:39.850 --> 01:20:43.653
Mom... is in the hospital again.


01:20:43.753 --> 01:20:47.084
- Jesus Christ.
- Yeah.


01:20:51.100 --> 01:20:54.097
What you got yourself into now, Jimmy?


01:20:54.197 --> 01:20:56.600
It's been all over TV. All night long.


01:20:56.700 --> 01:21:00.371
Showin' your picture. Cops come here.
Asking me, have I seen you?


01:21:00.471 --> 01:21:03.972
Do I know where you guys are,
both of yous?


01:21:04.072 --> 01:21:06.654
So, what's going on?


01:21:07.477 --> 01:21:11.514
I'll need your car.
Mike and I need to lay low for a while.


01:21:11.844 --> 01:21:16.187
It wasn't enough that you ruined
your own fuckin' life?


01:21:16.287 --> 01:21:18.956
Now you're gonna bring Michael
into this?


01:21:19.056 --> 01:21:21.961
I'm not bringing Michael into anything.
I'm trying to get him out.


01:21:22.061 --> 01:21:26.563
- Who you running from this time?
- Shawn Maguire.


01:21:27.363 --> 01:21:29.210
I killed his son.


01:21:29.966 --> 01:21:31.788
I killed Danny.


01:21:35.172 --> 01:21:37.074
Get the fuck out of my house!


01:21:37.574 --> 01:21:38.408
Get the fuck out of here!


01:21:38.508 --> 01:21:40.249
It's not his fault this time.
He's trying to get me out of this.


01:21:40.349 --> 01:21:42.980
No, he's not trying to get you
out of this, Michael. He's not.


01:21:43.080 --> 01:21:46.950
He's only loyal to one person.
He's gonna turn you over to Shawn.


01:21:47.050 --> 01:21:49.019
I'm his son. He's not gonna
turn me over to Shawn.


01:21:49.119 --> 01:21:52.890
He killed his own cousin
for Shawn Maguire.


01:21:54.090 --> 01:21:57.695
- What the fuck you talkin' about?
- I'm talking about your cousin Billy.


01:22:01.865 --> 01:22:06.203
No. Roy Demeo's guys killed Billy.
Everybody knows that.


01:22:06.303 --> 01:22:10.162
For God's sake, Jimmy.
Tell your son the truth.


01:22:12.142 --> 01:22:13.944
<i>Billy had problems.</i>


01:22:14.044 --> 01:22:16.880
<i>Yeah. Sure. Billy had problems.</i>


01:22:16.980 --> 01:22:19.316
<i>He couldn't quite quit the dope.</i>


01:22:19.416 --> 01:22:22.253
<i>Billy used to follow Jimmy
and Shawn around everywhere.</i>


01:22:22.553 --> 01:22:25.822
<i>He thought they were some kind
of goddamn heroes.</i>


01:22:25.922 --> 01:22:29.826
<i>And then the night he got pinched,
the D.A. wanted him to rat out Shawn.</i>


01:22:29.926 --> 01:22:32.426
<i>Otherwise, they were gonna
lock him up for ten years.</i>


01:22:32.526 --> 01:22:37.234
<i>And he's just a kid, and he's scared
to death. And he was gonna talk.</i>


01:22:37.334 --> 01:22:42.172
But Jimmy, he wasn't gonna let
that happen. Were you, Jimmy?


01:22:47.744 --> 01:22:50.948
I had to tell the boy.
He can't trust you.


01:22:51.748 --> 01:22:53.267
Mike!


01:22:53.367 --> 01:22:55.916
Mike! Wait!


01:22:56.753 --> 01:22:59.823
Michael. Wait. Michael!


01:23:08.131 --> 01:23:09.906
Here.


01:23:10.006 --> 01:23:13.203
Whose side are you gonna choose
this time, Jimmy?


01:23:31.653 --> 01:23:33.057
E.R.


01:23:33.157 --> 01:23:35.692
Yeah, Cheryl's off tonight.


01:23:55.579 --> 01:23:56.974
Ma.


01:24:12.729 --> 01:24:14.397
Ma.


01:25:36.979 --> 01:25:40.550
- We heard from Price?
- Not yet.


01:25:52.028 --> 01:25:54.898
- Is it done?
- <i>Not yet, Shawn.</i>


01:25:54.998 --> 01:25:58.169
I'm giving you one more chance
to walk away from this.


01:26:00.447 --> 01:26:04.307
- You're giving me one more chance?
- <i>That's right.</i>


01:26:04.407 --> 01:26:08.288
As long as you're comin' after Michael,
I'm comin' after you.


01:26:08.388 --> 01:26:12.783
- <i>Walk away, Shawn.</i>
- Walk away to what, Jimmy?


01:26:13.764 --> 01:26:15.686
Ain't got nothing left
to walk back to anymore.


01:26:16.286 --> 01:26:18.922
This is between you and me.
Leave my son out of it.


01:26:19.022 --> 01:26:20.341
Fuck you.


01:26:23.459 --> 01:26:25.495
Then we do like you always said.


01:26:25.995 --> 01:26:29.861
We cross that line together. Right now.


01:26:45.749 --> 01:26:47.651
Tell everyone to get ready.


01:26:48.451 --> 01:26:50.377
Jimmy's comin'.


01:26:56.626 --> 01:26:59.597
- I'll take another, Terry.
- All right. One sec.


01:26:59.997 --> 01:27:01.031
Hey, Terry.


01:27:15.180 --> 01:27:16.620
You fuckin'...


01:27:42.506 --> 01:27:44.529
Drop it.


01:27:48.844 --> 01:27:51.348
Open the door. Come on. Move.


01:30:32.107 --> 01:30:35.312
Been a long night, Jimmy?


01:30:36.979 --> 01:30:38.161
Yeah.


01:30:40.294 --> 01:30:43.452
Growin' up, all we wanted
was to be like those guys


01:30:43.552 --> 01:30:46.955
we saw walkin' down
to their social clubs on tenth Avenue.


01:30:47.055 --> 01:30:49.359
Now look at us.


01:30:50.359 --> 01:30:53.831
I never wanted to be like those guys.


01:30:53.931 --> 01:30:57.501
All I wanted was to be like you, Shawn.


01:30:58.441 --> 01:31:01.470
I'm sorry, Jimmy.


01:32:31.227 --> 01:32:33.430
Shawn. Stop.


01:32:37.065 --> 01:32:39.619
Come on, Shawn.


01:33:42.598 --> 01:33:44.525
Ji...


01:34:36.419 --> 01:34:37.681
We got a walk-in.


01:34:37.781 --> 01:34:41.486
Young kid. Says he's got information
about Mike Conlon.


01:34:54.169 --> 01:34:55.468
<i>Get down!</i>


01:34:56.205 --> 01:34:57.840
Why didn't you bring this to me earlier?


01:34:58.040 --> 01:35:00.476
I thought they killed Mike
and maybe they were comin' after me.


01:35:00.776 --> 01:35:02.784
My little brother found me
at my friend's place


01:35:02.884 --> 01:35:05.982
and told me that Mike came by the apartment
and said he was in trouble.


01:35:06.082 --> 01:35:08.618
So... that's why I'm here.


01:35:08.718 --> 01:35:10.620
Can you tell me how you know Mike again?


01:35:10.720 --> 01:35:13.022
Trains me down at the gym on fourth ave.


01:35:13.122 --> 01:35:16.627
They... they got a program for kids
who don't got dads.


01:35:18.927 --> 01:35:20.455
He's my mentor.


01:35:23.182 --> 01:35:24.867
All right. Sit tight.
I'll be right back.


01:35:24.967 --> 01:35:27.036
Call ballistics. Tell 'em to check
Danny Maguire's gun.


01:35:27.136 --> 01:35:29.906
See if it matches the bullets
in the Albanians the patrol found earlier.


01:35:30.006 --> 01:35:31.774
- All right. Got it.
- Call for you, Harding. Line two.


01:35:31.874 --> 01:35:34.177
- Tell 'em I left for the night.
- It's Michael Conlon.


01:35:34.477 --> 01:35:36.898
Says he wants to turn himself in.


01:35:41.116 --> 01:35:42.157
Michael.


01:35:51.894 --> 01:35:55.265
- I won the first round, so...
- You won the first round?


01:35:55.365 --> 01:35:56.699
Green!


01:35:56.799 --> 01:35:59.102
Catching up to me.


01:36:08.711 --> 01:36:09.659
You lose!


01:36:14.783 --> 01:36:16.505
I'm getting over here.


01:36:17.894 --> 01:36:21.791
What the fuck are you doin' here?
Cops are on their way.


01:36:22.091 --> 01:36:23.977
I'd get the hell out of here,
if I were you.


01:36:24.077 --> 01:36:26.048
I'm too old to run.


01:36:27.533 --> 01:36:30.403
Where the hell would I go anyway?


01:36:31.133 --> 01:36:32.668
It's over, Michael.


01:36:33.368 --> 01:36:36.673
You and your family don't have to worry
about Shawn no more.


01:36:37.273 --> 01:36:41.143
When the cops get here, I'll tell them
everything they wanna hear.


01:36:41.243 --> 01:36:44.148
That you... didn't have
any part in all this.


01:36:47.449 --> 01:36:50.720
You mi... you mind if I wait inside?


01:36:52.720 --> 01:36:55.258
The girls are still in there.


01:36:56.172 --> 01:36:59.028
Yeah. Right.


01:37:04.367 --> 01:37:06.869
It's nice to finally meet you.
I'm Gabriela.


01:37:08.393 --> 01:37:10.312
Hi.


01:37:11.573 --> 01:37:14.260
Nice to meet you, too, Gabriela.


01:37:14.810 --> 01:37:15.711
Why don't we go inside.


01:37:15.811 --> 01:37:17.781
- Babe.
- Let's go inside.


01:37:24.954 --> 01:37:26.929
Okay.


01:37:31.560 --> 01:37:32.996
Girls?


01:37:34.821 --> 01:37:38.506
Girls. This is your grandfather.


01:37:39.468 --> 01:37:40.920
Hi. My name's Catelyn.


01:37:41.020 --> 01:37:45.625
Well, hi, Catelyn. I'm Jimmy.
Nice to meet ya. You're a pretty girl.


01:37:45.725 --> 01:37:48.577
Why were you standing
by my house earlier?


01:37:51.889 --> 01:37:53.024
I was waitin' on your dad.


01:37:53.124 --> 01:37:54.967
- Did you get all wet?
- Oh, just a little.


01:37:55.067 --> 01:37:57.086
Wanna say hi to your grandfather?


01:37:57.386 --> 01:38:01.461
- Could we go feed the ducks now, Mommy?
- Come on. Let's go put your coats on.


01:38:09.498 --> 01:38:11.267
- Okay, Lily, you got the bread?
- Yep.


01:38:11.367 --> 01:38:13.369
- You're gonna hold on to it?
- Got it!


01:38:13.469 --> 01:38:16.304
You have to give some
to your sister, too, okay?


01:38:16.404 --> 01:38:19.776
- No, I won't eat it.
- Let's go.


01:38:19.876 --> 01:38:22.828
- I'm gonna go and keep 'em busy.
- Okay. All right.


01:38:22.928 --> 01:38:25.215
I don't want the girls to be here
when the cops come around.


01:38:25.315 --> 01:38:28.140
Yeah. Yeah, they shouldn't see that.


01:38:32.188 --> 01:38:34.210
Goodbye, Michael.


01:38:48.704 --> 01:38:51.007
- Duckie.
- Remember to walk really slowly, okay?


01:38:51.107 --> 01:38:53.406
You don't want to scare them.


01:40:11.888 --> 01:40:13.955
You okay?


01:40:15.858 --> 01:40:17.825
Roll...


01:40:20.366 --> 01:40:22.065
I gotta go back up there.


01:40:24.533 --> 01:40:26.636
It's for me.


01:40:26.736 --> 01:40:29.808
- Okay.
- I'll be right back.


01:40:51.994 --> 01:40:53.964
- Get the girls out of here.
- Come on, let's go.


01:41:21.990 --> 01:41:23.723
Stay quiet, honey. Stay quiet.


01:41:37.639 --> 01:41:39.041
Oh, God.


01:42:30.593 --> 01:42:34.163
Where's Daddy? I'm scared.


01:42:40.102 --> 01:42:42.517
It's okay, honey.
You have to be quiet-quiet.


01:43:52.578 --> 01:43:54.629
Gabriela, run!


01:45:41.884 --> 01:45:44.944
You should have killed me
when you had the chance.


01:46:16.411 --> 01:46:17.442
Dad?


01:46:19.424 --> 01:46:21.285
Dad?


01:46:35.431 --> 01:46:38.299
Mike! Put that gun down!


01:46:38.399 --> 01:46:41.210
- I'm innocent! I didn't do anything!
- I know. I know.


01:46:41.550 --> 01:46:43.328
I need you to put the gun down.


01:47:01.069 --> 01:47:04.346
Get on the outside, Legs.
Get on the outside.


01:47:04.446 --> 01:47:06.501
Get off the ropes, Legs.
Get off the ropes.


01:47:06.601 --> 01:47:08.935
There you go. Roll to the left.
Get outta there.


01:47:09.035 --> 01:47:12.349
Check him with a jab. There you go.
There you go. Quick feet.


01:47:12.941 --> 01:47:15.911
- Yes!
- Two! Three!


01:47:16.011 --> 01:47:18.747
- He's done.
- Four! Five! It's over!


01:47:19.047 --> 01:47:23.085
That's what I'm talking about.
Beautiful! Now get in the middle.


01:47:28.324 --> 01:47:30.392
You're gonna get a big, big sugar rush.


01:47:30.492 --> 01:47:33.399
Take the nose. Put that there,
like this. There you go.


01:47:33.499 --> 01:47:35.664
- What's that supposed to be, Cate?
- Frosty the snowman, duh.


01:47:35.764 --> 01:47:38.401
- Duh! What about you, sweetheart?
- Rudolph the reindeer.


01:47:38.501 --> 01:47:41.804
- He's so pretty I might have to take a bite.
- No, Daddy! It's mine!


01:47:41.904 --> 01:47:44.506
Okay, I won't do anything.


01:47:44.606 --> 01:47:48.514
- I gotta go get ready for work.
- Don't take all of them.


01:47:48.538 --> 01:47:50.538



01:47:50.562 --> 01:47:52.562
<font color="#008040">Enjoy Your Life </font>
